Subject: [PATCH v3 1/2] coresight: Fix clock refcount imbalance on platform remove

Backport of Jie Gan's July 10 v3 series, patch 1/2:
https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/07/10/62

Resume platform devices before teardown to balance the devm-managed clock
release. Disable runtime PM, set suspended and drop the remove usage vote.
The companion TNOC platform-remove patch is inapplicable to 6.18's AMBA-only
TNOC driver; its source is preserved separately as upstream evidence.

Fixes: 1abc1b212eff ("coresight: Appropriately disable programming clocks")
Signed-off-by: Jie Gan <jie.gan@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-catu.c b/drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-catu.c
index ad8dafea7d2f..b72fa7f4bdeb 100644
--- a/drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-catu.c
+++ b/drivers/hwtracing/coresight/coresight-catu.c
@@ -646,8 +646,16 @@ static void catu_platform_remove(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (WARN_ON(!drvdata))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * Resume the device so its clocks are enabled again, balancing the
+	 * clk_disable_unprepare() that devm runs when the driver detaches.
+	 * Then mark it suspended and drop the usage count taken here.
+	 */
+	pm_runtime_get_sync(&pdev->dev);
 	__catu_remove(&pdev->dev);
 	pm_runtime_disable(&pdev->dev);
+	pm_runtime_set_suspended(&pdev->dev);
+	pm_runtime_put_noidle(&pdev->dev);
 }
 
